# Machine-specific settings. Copy and edit locally:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The runtime is selected by PYTHON_HOME. Either set it directly and leave
# CONDA_HOME / ENV_NAME empty, or leave it empty and let CONDA_HOME + ENV_NAME
# derive it as $CONDA_HOME/envs/$ENV_NAME. An explicit PYTHON_HOME always wins.
# Fill in CODE_NAME, then EITHER PYTHON_HOME alone, OR CONDA_HOME + ENV_NAME.
# Leave the keys of the route you are not using empty — a leftover placeholder
# is read as a real path and fails.
CODE_NAME=YOUR_CODE_NAME
ENV_NAME=
CONDA_HOME=
PYTHON_HOME=

# Optional. Upstream repo execs/update.sh pulls skills, hooks, and workflow
# guides from — point it at a fork to update from there instead. Resolution is
# environment first, then this file, then the default below.
STAR_REPOSITORY=https://github.com/wanghao9610/STAR.git

# Optional. Which agent harness trees execs/update.sh installs and keeps current,
# comma separated: claude, codex, cursor, dsh, kimi, pi, qwen — or all, which is
# the default, or none for the shared skeleton by itself. A tree left out is
# never written and never deleted, so whatever the project already has there
# stays. Resolution is environment first, then this file; --harnesses overrides both
# for one run.
STAR_HARNESSES=

# Optional. How much the STAR skills ask before deciding (workflow conventions
# §7.7): low = take the recommended option on judgment calls and log it, commit
# without asking and name each commit in the reply (§1.5), and in Claude Code
# skip the permission prompt before each file edit and approve the executor's
# plan-mode prompt into auto mode; medium = ask as documented
# (default); high = confirm item by item. Hard gates — the STOP line, deletions,
# overwrites — are asked at every level.
INVOLVE=medium

# Optional. Language the agents reply in and newly generated workflow
# documents (plans, reports) are written in (workflow conventions §7.6):
# en or zh. Unset or empty = follow the conversation's language; an explicit
# in-conversation request overrides it. Existing documents keep the language
# declared in their frontmatter — STAR_LANG never rewrites them.
STAR_LANG=

# Optional. Which model runs each tier of STAR work, on a harness that can
# start a delegate on a named model (Claude Code: fable / opus / sonnet /
# haiku, or a full model id). PLAN = research judgment: plans, reviews,
# analyses, blind reads. EXEC = implementation and production. READ =
# read-only scans, collectors, summaries. Empty = the harness default, the
# session's own model, and nothing about how a skill runs changes.
#
# A value is either one model name, used by whichever harness reads it, or
# comma-separated <harness>:<model> entries so one .env serves every tree —
# the tags are STAR_HARNESSES' own: claude, codex, cursor, dsh, kimi, pi,
# qwen. A run takes the entry tagged with the tree it runs from, falls back to
# an untagged entry, and reads the key as empty when it has neither; a tag no
# tree answers to is ignored, which is the room a harness added later fits in.
# The model name is spelled the way its own harness spells one — a Pi entry
# carries the provider (pi:anthropic/claude-fable-5), a Claude one an alias or
# a full id — and a name containing a colon must be tagged, since the first
# colon is where the tag ends. Claude Code, a Codex runtime exposing a model
# selector, Kimi with a selectable secondary-model pool, and STAR's Pi extension
# pass the model on each dispatch. Cursor and Qwen use the named STAR agents:
# run `bash execs/update.sh --models` after editing these keys, then start a new
# session. Qwen entries are model ids or authType:modelId, not model grades.
# DSH currently keeps its existing model because its tool has no selector.
# Unavailable models or interfaces keep the current execution route and report
# why; no model names are translated between providers. Full rule: workflow
# conventions §10.8 and each skill's harness-specific dispatch paragraph.
#
# Example: STAR_PLAN_MODEL=fable, STAR_EXEC_MODEL=opus, STAR_READ_MODEL=sonnet
# — or, across trees: STAR_PLAN_MODEL=claude:fable,codex:gpt-6-astra
# Bare Claude aliases apply to every reader; tag them claude: when sharing .env.
STAR_PLAN_MODEL=
STAR_EXEC_MODEL=
STAR_READ_MODEL=
